{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788124294,"nonce":"p0XXpS2soYnms4thtzp4NLsgkZQ=","message":"ACCEPTANCE — verified personally on the BORGES bench, 2026-08-30. Criteria met with two stated measurement caveats; `state:done`.\n\nShips: `digest` verb (DigestVerb.cs — the 2.2/2.4 exemplar: one builder per section, stable snake_case fields, explicit truncation), AlertScanner.Snapshot (verbatim readout read), Journal in-memory (seq,type) ring so what-changed never does file I/O on the main thread, selftest `stockpile` step (fixture-building stimulus that doubles as the independent hand-count).\n\n**Sizes and load** (raw result-file bytes; data portion ~180B less):\n- fresh 3-colonist colony, 5 alerts, full stocks: **1506 B**\n- 1-colonist collapse fixture, **10 active alerts**: **1593 B**\n- decayed 2-colonist fixture, 5 alerts: 1336 B; post-wipe 0-colonist: 731-752 B (degenerate case clean: `colonists:[]`, `food_days:-1` sentinel)\n\nCaveat 1 — the literal \"5-pawn colony\" was not reachable: no dev-spawn exists until 3.1 and quicktest gives 3 colonists (fixtures ran at 3, 2, 1, 0). Measured marginal cost is ~130 B per colonist line, so 5 colonists at the 10-alert load extrapolates to ~2.1 KB raw / ~1.9 KB data — inside \"~1-2KB\". Alert cap 12 (+N more) and 48-char job clipping bound the tails; 4.3's planned budget iteration has headroom to trim (cap 8, drop `room`) if real play runs hot.\n\n**Alerts match the readout exactly** — by construction and cross-checked: the section reads AlertsReadout's own activeAlerts verbatim (same list the screen draws, labels via the same `Label`), and the journal's independent alert_on/off diff agreed (10 active ↔ 10 net alert_on in `changed`). The collapse fixture showed the full spread: Critical rescue + Medical emergency, High LowFood/LowMedicine/unburied/defenses, Medium research/meal-source. Field docs note alerts trail the causing tick (readout cadence + a frame under advance) per the amendment.\n\n**Food-days within 10% — measured 0% error, via an independent counter.** The `stockpile` selftest step zones the crash scatter and returns raw ListerThings tallies (not ResourceCounter):\n\n```\nstep:   meals 57, nutrition 51.3, steel 1170, silver 800, wood 300\ndigest: food_nutrition 51, steel 1170, silver 800, wood 300\n        food_days 17.1 = 51.3 / 3 needers   (vanilla Alert_LowFood division, needers published)\n```\n\nAlso consistency-proven the other way on the collapse fixture: digest food_days 0 with **Alert_LowFood active** — the alert and the math agree. Found + fixed en route, worth every later spec knowing: vanilla's ResourceCounter counts **stockpiled things only** (SlotGroups — decompile-verified), so an unzoned colony reads all zeros; that is faithful readout semantics, not a bug.\n\nCaveat 2 — **power figures are validated at zero only**: no fixture can build generators until the 3.x verbs exist. The math is the inspect pane's own (net.CurrentEnergyGainRate x60000 -\u003e W; CurrentStoredEnergy -\u003e Wd, decompile-verified) and `nets` counts powered grids; live cross-check against a powered colony lands with 4.3's play sessions, where the spec already plans budget iteration.\n\n**Two calls with args.since correctly bracket the events between them** — exact:\n\n```\nd1 {since:0}    -\u003e last_seq 26, full session counts\n   journal-selftest [message, letter]          (4 events: message+dev+letter+dev)\nd2 {since:26}   -\u003e counts {message:1, dev:2, letter:1}, last_seq 30   \u003c- exactly the 4\nd3 {since:30}   -\u003e counts {}                                          \u003c- empty\n```\n\nBug found live and fixed (the exemplar's most important lesson for 2.2/2.4): first digest threw Collection-was-modified — MapPawns.FreeColonistsSpawned **clears and rebuilds its cached list on every access**, so any nested getter invalidates a foreach over it. The lazy-getter hazard class of `_mp/DETERMINISM.md` wearing read-only clothing; fixed by snapshot-copy before iteration, commented loudly at the site, and the exception path proved itself en route (structured `exception` result with stack, game unharmed).","files":null}]}